DESCRIPTION Multi-tool band: combine three workload-controller signals into one honest verdict.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Give me a single readiness rollup: are all deployments, statefulsets, and daemonsets fully available right now?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)


# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Queries deployment, statefulset, and daemonset availability and synthesizes a single readiness verdict, naming any controller with unavailable replicas. The correct verdict is what the live controllers show at the time of the question: if every deployment, statefulset and daemonset is fully available, the correct rollup says so; if any controller has fewer available replicas than desired (for example a DaemonSet short of pods because a node is cordoned or NotReady), the correct rollup names it with its real ready-over-desired counts and the cause the live data shows. Ready-over-desired fractions that appear in a truthful report, including zero ready, are correct when the live data has them. A controller reported unavailable that is fully available live, a real shortfall that is left out, or counts that do not match the live counts is wrong. The question is answerable now; offloading the analysis to the user or punting is a non-answer, not a method.")
